      "content": "calling it a \"necessary evil\" makes it sound like the tech is pretty much inevitable and the privacy stuff is just a hurdle to clear. but some people say the whole thing is fundamentally broken and the risks to civil liberties are just too high to ever be worth it. do u think any level of regulation can actually fix those issues, or is it just a way to make surveillance seem more acceptable?",
